  "body": "## Summary\n\nRetain a matched PlaceToPay/PayPhone approval that arrives after local checkout expiry/cancellation without reopening fulfillment, posting a capture or issuing a receipt.\n\n- Append exact observed money and immutable references to a deduplicated reconciliation exception and correlated audit.\n- Keep subsequent matched queries on hold; exception workflow-label edits are not financial-release authority.\n- Preserve historical operation/attempt/intent/checkout data. Recovery projects the held operation as ambiguous, hides its old redirect and never permits fallback.\n- Avoid an additional generic scheduled-query exception for the same recorded approval.\n- Add database, API and web regressions plus ADR 0124, test evidence and operator/rollback procedures.\n\n## Dependency and review order\n\n**Depends on #378** (`codex/payment-capture-replay-integrity-20260915`) and its documented #374 \u2192 #371 \u2192 #363 \u2192 earlier payment stack. This is deliberately a dependent draft; do not merge or activate independently. Root main is `6f67081a73e66e422f331cb31c455a78977a400e`; its separate messaging/artwork/catalog changes and the parent stack's refreshed test/catalog additions remain merge dependencies, not overwritten changes.\n\nMobile #81 remains pinned at `d84fc3196202f2ac2468f78816b3c98fb4a22144`. No mobile/gitlink/OpenAPI/generated-client changes in this increment. Its separate social-contract lineage still needs coordinated generation after merging.\n\n## Verification\n\nFinal frozen source: `88e75b536d5dc0401c6e722e23f6beaf626dff38`; subsequent commit changes documentation only. Local macOS, Stack lts-24.42/GHC 9.10.3, PostgreSQL 16.10, Node 24.8.0. All provider evidence and account fixtures are synthetic; **no real sandbox success is claimed**.\n\n- `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --rerun-tests`: **2,596 examples, zero failures**.\n- `TDF_PROVIDER_RETRY_DATABASE_URL='<isolated local test database>' sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh`: **198 examples, zero failures**, plus repeat-apply, empty rollback/flag retention/reapply and populated-rollback refusal checks. Full exact safe local command and timestamps are in the evidence document.\n- `npm --prefix tdf-hq-ui test -- --runTestsByPath src/components/payments/HostedProviderCheckout.test.tsx src/pages/ProviderPaymentReturnPage.test.tsx`: **14 tests, two suites passed**.\n- `npm --prefix tdf-hq-ui run typecheck`: passed.\n- `npm run quality:repo`: passed, **157 Node tests** and repository/formal/generated-drift gates.\n- Catalog audit: passed, **1,422 files, 1,128 candidates, zero unreviewed/stale decisions**. No catalog decisions or gates changed.\n- Generated web/mobile files compare identical; diff whitespace and new relative documentation links verified.\n\nThe report preserves the red-test history, including a corrected test-only SQL alias error. All three private Unix-socket test clusters were stopped and independently verified stopped; logs/data retained. No screenshots, native-device tests or full production-schema rehearsal were produced by this increment.\n\n## Migration / rollout / rollback\n\nNo new SQL migration, backfill, feature activation or historical-reference rewrite. Existing parent query-recovery schema remains prerequisite. UUIDv5 review identity uses the existing exception primary key; it is not an authentication token.\n\nDrain old query/callback consumers before rollout: old binaries do not enforce the held recovery projection. Roll back a binary only with these consumers disabled and affected orders held. Retain review/audit history; never delete evidence, set paid, reopen inventory or create a replacement payment to bypass the hold.\n\n## Risks / remaining gates\n\n- This exception is **observed approval evidence, not a capture/suspense ledger, settlement or refund**. A compliant finance/fulfillment remediation and release command is still missing.\n- New handling applies to shared PlaceToPay/PayPhone query reconciliation. Datafast/PayPal shared capture regressions pass, but their first-late-payment operational workflow is not newly implemented here.\n- Existing admin reconciliation view is an aggregate, not a complete cash ledger or individual review-resolution interface.\n- Staging read-only inspector still reports `hosting_authentication_unavailable`, `sourceCommit=null`, `providerQualified=false`, despite healthy public endpoints. Restore authorized Fly staging access; then verify exact SHA, sandbox aliases, secret names and provider/webhook configuration.\n- No staging/provider transaction, production deployment, live charge, refund or payout was performed. Provider contracts/sandboxes, legal/accounting/PCI approval, remaining subscriptions/marketplace/settlement flows and mobile lineage reconciliation remain open.\n\nEvidence: `docs/payments/closed-checkout-approval-2026-09-15.md`; architecture/threat invariants: `docs/adr/0124-closed-checkout-approval-evidence.md`.\n",
